      "message": "The flipside of this is that host OS independent (i.e. java) members ought to have a single generic \"host\" target instead of the specific host OS type. I looked into that a bit, but noticed that e.g. java_library_host can produce several prebuilts for host: https://android.git.corp.google.com/platform/prebuilts/runtime/+/refs/heads/master/mainline/conscrypt/host-exports/Android.bp#31\n\nThe jars are identical there, but I think a proper solution should verify that (or better introduce \"CommonHostOs\" as an OsType with its own variant in osMutator and use that instead of the specific host OS), and that meant a bit more work than I was prepared to spend on this.\n\nI did put together a test for it anyway: https://r.android.com/1365637",
